From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] qcom_rnd: qcom,prng-ee on arm64 (the SM6115's PRNG)

FreeBSD's qcom_rnd knew only "qcom,prng" on the IPQ4018 (ARMv7). The
SM6115 (F(x)tec Pro1X) has the PRNG's execution environment window
("qcom,prng-ee" at 0x1b53000): TrustZone set it up and owns its
configuration, its AHB clock is a voted branch in the GCC. Read as
Linux's qcom-rng reads it (qcom_rnd_ee.h): the clock voted on around each
read with clk-branch.c's checks, a word whenever STATUS has one (10 ms
at most), a word of zero or the same word twice fails the read; three
failed reads in a row and the source gives nothing any more. Counters
under dev.qcom_rnd.0. Built for arm64 (files.arm64) as "device qcom_rnd".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/sys/conf/files.arm64
+++ b/sys/conf/files.arm64
@@ -733,6 +733,7 @@
 # Qualcomm
 arm64/qualcomm/qcom_gcc.c			optional qcom_gcc fdt
 dev/qcom_wdt/qcom_wdt.c				optional qcom_wdt fdt
+dev/qcom_rnd/qcom_rnd.c				optional qcom_rnd fdt
 dev/ufshci/ufshci_fdt.c				optional ufshci fdt
 dev/qcom_tlmm/qcom_tlmm_sm6115.c		optional qcom_tlmm_sm6115 fdt gpio
 dev/iicbus/goodix.c				optional goodix fdt gpio evdev
--- a/sys/dev/qcom_rnd/qcom_rnd.c
+++ b/sys/dev/qcom_rnd/qcom_rnd.c
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
